window.LC_CHUNKS=window.LC_CHUNKS||{};window.LC_CHUNKS["school_computer_science_en"]=window.LC_CHUNKS["school_computer_science_en"]||{};window.LC_CHUNKS["school_computer_science_en"][11]={"school_computer_science_en:M11-L1":"<article class=\"lesson-standard\"><h1 id=\"L1\">M11-L1 – Singly linked lists<\/h1>\n<p><strong>Course area:<\/strong> M11 – Linked structures and graph search<\/p>\n<p><strong>Level:<\/strong> Upper secondary (basic level)<\/p>\n<p><strong>Prior knowledge:<\/strong> <a\nhref=\"index.html?course=school_computer-science&amp;module=M6&amp;lesson=L1&amp;syslang=en&amp;doclang=en&amp;theme=light\">M6-L1<\/a>; <a\nhref=\"index.html?course=school_computer-science&amp;module=M6&amp;lesson=L4&amp;syslang=en&amp;doclang=en&amp;theme=light\">M6-L4<\/a><\/p>\n<p><strong>Curriculum context:<\/strong> Basic-level extension based on\nBavaria’s Grade 12 curriculum; not a nationwide uniform requirement.<\/p>\n<h2 id=\"S1\"><span class=\"section-number\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><\/span>Learning objectives<\/h2>\n<p>Model a singly linked list as a sequence of objects, distinguish data\nfrom references, implement recursive search, insertion, removal and\nlength, and explain their cost. Test empty lists, changes of head and\ninvalid positions.<\/p>\n<h2 id=\"S2\"><span class=\"section-number\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><\/span>Nodes and the list invariant<\/h2>\n<p>A node stores a payload and a reference to its successor. The head\nvariable <code>head<\/code> refers to the first node; <code>None<\/code>\ndenotes an empty list or the end of the chain. In our model the chain\nreachable from <code>head<\/code> is finite and acyclic. A node storing 4\nwith a successor storing 9 represents the sequence [4, 9], not two\nadjacent memory addresses. References connect objects independently of\ntheir physical locations. Separating payload from linkage allows us to\nstore book records instead of numbers later.<\/p>\n<p>An empty list is also the base case of a recursive structure: a\nnonempty list consists of its head and a remainder, which is itself a\nlist.<\/p>\n<h2 id=\"S3\"><span class=\"section-number\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><\/span>Insertion and removal<\/h2>\n<p>Inserting at position 1 in [4, 9] first creates a new node with value\n7 and successor 9. The node storing 4 then points to the new node.\nOverwriting the old reference before preserving it could lose the rest\nof the chain. Positions start at 0; for length n, n is a valid insertion\nposition. Removing the first matching value 4 makes its former successor\nthe new head. The caller must retain the returned head. Duplicate values\nare allowed; removal affects only the first match.<\/p>\n<figure>\n<img src=\"../learning-courses-school-computer-science-en/media/img/S_COS_046_EN.svg\"\nalt=\"Before head → 4 → 9 → None; after head → 4 → 7 → 9 → None.\" />\n<figcaption>Figure: Before head → 4 → 9 → None; after head → 4 → 7 → 9 →\nNone.<\/figcaption>\n<\/figure>\n<h2 id=\"S4\"><span class=\"section-number\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><\/span>Recursive operations in Python<\/h2>\n<p>The class represents the object structure; functions implement the\nlist operations. <code>insert_at<\/code> returns the possibly changed\nhead. An invalid index raises an exception. <code>remove_first<\/code>\nreturns the unchanged chain if the value is absent. Copy the whole block\nand execute it in Python 3. Assertions fail if a result is\nincorrect.<\/p>\n<div class=\"sourceCode\" id=\"cb1\"><pre\nclass=\"sourceCode python\"><code class=\"sourceCode python\"><span id=\"cb1-1\"><a href=\"#cb1-1\" aria-hidden=\"true\" tabindex=\"-1\"><\/a><span class=\"kw\">class<\/span> Node:<\/span>\n<span id=\"cb1-2\"><a href=\"#cb1-2\" aria-hidden=\"true\" tabindex=\"-1\"><\/a>    <span class=\"kw\">def<\/span> <span class=\"fu\">__init__<\/span>(<span class=\"va\">self<\/span>, value, next_node<span class=\"op\">=<\/span><span class=\"va\">None<\/span>):<\/span>\n<span id=\"cb1-3\"><a href=\"#cb1-3\" aria-hidden=\"true\" tabindex=\"-1\"><\/a>        <span class=\"va\">self<\/span>.value <span class=\"op\">=<\/span> value<\/span>\n<span id=\"cb1-4\"><a href=\"#cb1-4\" aria-hidden=\"true\" tabindex=\"-1\"><\/a>        <span class=\"va\">self<\/span>.<span class=\"bu\">next<\/span> <span class=\"op\">=<\/span> next_node<\/span>\n<span id=\"cb1-5\"><a href=\"#cb1-5\" aria-hidden=\"true\" tabindex=\"-1\"><\/a><\/span>\n<span id=\"cb1-6\"><a href=\"#cb1-6\" aria-hidden=\"true\" tabindex=\"-1\"><\/a><\/span>\n<span id=\"cb1-7\"><a href=\"#cb1-7\" aria-hidden=\"true\" tabindex=\"-1\"><\/a><span class=\"kw\">def<\/span> contains(node, value):<\/span>\n<span id=\"cb1-8\"><a href=\"#cb1-8\" aria-hidden=\"true\" tabindex=\"-1\"><\/a>    <span class=\"cf\">if<\/span> node <span class=\"kw\">is<\/span> <span class=\"va\">None<\/span>:<\/span>\n<span id=\"cb1-9\"><a href=\"#cb1-9\" aria-hidden=\"true\" tabindex=\"-1\"><\/a>        <span class=\"cf\">return<\/span> <span class=\"va\">False<\/span><\/span>\n<span id=\"cb1-10\"><a href=\"#cb1-10\" aria-hidden=\"true\" tabindex=\"-1\"><\/a>    <span class=\"cf\">return<\/span> node.value <span class=\"op\">==<\/span> value <span class=\"kw\">or<\/span> contains(node.<span class=\"bu\">next<\/span>, value)<\/span>\n<span id=\"cb1-11\"><a href=\"#cb1-11\" aria-hidden=\"true\" tabindex=\"-1\"><\/a><\/span>\n<span id=\"cb1-12\"><a href=\"#cb1-12\" aria-hidden=\"true\" tabindex=\"-1\"><\/a><\/span>\n<span id=\"cb1-13\"><a href=\"#cb1-13\" aria-hidden=\"true\" tabindex=\"-1\"><\/a><span class=\"kw\">def<\/span> length(node):<\/span>\n<span id=\"cb1-14\"><a href=\"#cb1-14\" aria-hidden=\"true\" tabindex=\"-1\"><\/a>    <span class=\"cf\">return<\/span> <span class=\"dv\">0<\/span> <span class=\"cf\">if<\/span> node <span class=\"kw\">is<\/span> <span class=\"va\">None<\/span> <span class=\"cf\">else<\/span> <span class=\"dv\">1<\/span> <span class=\"op\">+<\/span> length(node.<span class=\"bu\">next<\/span>)<\/span>\n<span id=\"cb1-15\"><a href=\"#cb1-15\" aria-hidden=\"true\" tabindex=\"-1\"><\/a><\/span>\n<span id=\"cb1-16\"><a href=\"#cb1-16\" aria-hidden=\"true\" tabindex=\"-1\"><\/a><\/span>\n<span id=\"cb1-17\"><a href=\"#cb1-17\" aria-hidden=\"true\" tabindex=\"-1\"><\/a><span class=\"kw\">def<\/span> insert_at(node, index, value):<\/span>\n<span id=\"cb1-18\"><a href=\"#cb1-18\" aria-hidden=\"true\" tabindex=\"-1\"><\/a>    <span class=\"cf\">if<\/span> index <span class=\"op\">&lt;<\/span> <span class=\"dv\">0<\/span>:<\/span>\n<span id=\"cb1-19\"><a href=\"#cb1-19\" aria-hidden=\"true\" tabindex=\"-1\"><\/a>        <span class=\"cf\">raise<\/span> <span class=\"pp\">IndexError<\/span>(index)<\/span>\n<span id=\"cb1-20\"><a href=\"#cb1-20\" aria-hidden=\"true\" tabindex=\"-1\"><\/a>    <span class=\"cf\">if<\/span> index <span class=\"op\">==<\/span> <span class=\"dv\">0<\/span>:<\/span>\n<span id=\"cb1-21\"><a href=\"#cb1-21\" aria-hidden=\"true\" tabindex=\"-1\"><\/a>        <span class=\"cf\">return<\/span> Node(value, node)<\/span>\n<span id=\"cb1-22\"><a href=\"#cb1-22\" aria-hidden=\"true\" tabindex=\"-1\"><\/a>    <span class=\"cf\">if<\/span> node <span class=\"kw\">is<\/span> <span class=\"va\">None<\/span>:<\/span>\n<span id=\"cb1-23\"><a href=\"#cb1-23\" aria-hidden=\"true\" tabindex=\"-1\"><\/a>        <span class=\"cf\">raise<\/span> <span class=\"pp\">IndexError<\/span>(index)<\/span>\n<span id=\"cb1-24\"><a href=\"#cb1-24\" aria-hidden=\"true\" tabindex=\"-1\"><\/a>    node.<span class=\"bu\">next<\/span> <span class=\"op\">=<\/span> insert_at(node.<span class=\"bu\">next<\/span>, index <span class=\"op\">-<\/span> <span class=\"dv\">1<\/span>, value)<\/span>\n<span id=\"cb1-25\"><a href=\"#cb1-25\" aria-hidden=\"true\" tabindex=\"-1\"><\/a>    <span class=\"cf\">return<\/span> node<\/span>\n<span id=\"cb1-26\"><a href=\"#cb1-26\" aria-hidden=\"true\" tabindex=\"-1\"><\/a><\/span>\n<span id=\"cb1-27\"><a href=\"#cb1-27\" aria-hidden=\"true\" tabindex=\"-1\"><\/a><\/span>\n<span id=\"cb1-28\"><a href=\"#cb1-28\" aria-hidden=\"true\" tabindex=\"-1\"><\/a><span class=\"kw\">def<\/span> remove_first(node, value):<\/span>\n<span id=\"cb1-29\"><a href=\"#cb1-29\" aria-hidden=\"true\" tabindex=\"-1\"><\/a>    <span class=\"cf\">if<\/span> node <span class=\"kw\">is<\/span> <span class=\"va\">None<\/span>:<\/span>\n<span id=\"cb1-30\"><a href=\"#cb1-30\" aria-hidden=\"true\" tabindex=\"-1\"><\/a>        <span class=\"cf\">return<\/span> <span class=\"va\">None<\/span><\/span>\n<span id=\"cb1-31\"><a href=\"#cb1-31\" aria-hidden=\"true\" tabindex=\"-1\"><\/a>    <span class=\"cf\">if<\/span> node.value <span class=\"op\">==<\/span> value:<\/span>\n<span id=\"cb1-32\"><a href=\"#cb1-32\" aria-hidden=\"true\" tabindex=\"-1\"><\/a>        <span class=\"cf\">return<\/span> node.<span class=\"bu\">next<\/span><\/span>\n<span id=\"cb1-33\"><a href=\"#cb1-33\" aria-hidden=\"true\" tabindex=\"-1\"><\/a>    node.<span class=\"bu\">next<\/span> <span class=\"op\">=<\/span> remove_first(node.<span class=\"bu\">next<\/span>, value)<\/span>\n<span id=\"cb1-34\"><a href=\"#cb1-34\" aria-hidden=\"true\" tabindex=\"-1\"><\/a>    <span class=\"cf\">return<\/span> node<\/span>\n<span id=\"cb1-35\"><a href=\"#cb1-35\" aria-hidden=\"true\" tabindex=\"-1\"><\/a><\/span>\n<span id=\"cb1-36\"><a href=\"#cb1-36\" aria-hidden=\"true\" tabindex=\"-1\"><\/a><\/span>\n<span id=\"cb1-37\"><a href=\"#cb1-37\" aria-hidden=\"true\" tabindex=\"-1\"><\/a><span class=\"kw\">def<\/span> values(node):<\/span>\n<span id=\"cb1-38\"><a href=\"#cb1-38\" aria-hidden=\"true\" tabindex=\"-1\"><\/a>    result <span class=\"op\">=<\/span> []<\/span>\n<span id=\"cb1-39\"><a href=\"#cb1-39\" aria-hidden=\"true\" tabindex=\"-1\"><\/a>    <span class=\"cf\">while<\/span> node <span class=\"kw\">is<\/span> <span class=\"kw\">not<\/span> <span class=\"va\">None<\/span>:<\/span>\n<span id=\"cb1-40\"><a href=\"#cb1-40\" aria-hidden=\"true\" tabindex=\"-1\"><\/a>        result.append(node.value)<\/span>\n<span id=\"cb1-41\"><a href=\"#cb1-41\" aria-hidden=\"true\" tabindex=\"-1\"><\/a>        node <span class=\"op\">=<\/span> node.<span class=\"bu\">next<\/span><\/span>\n<span id=\"cb1-42\"><a href=\"#cb1-42\" aria-hidden=\"true\" tabindex=\"-1\"><\/a>    <span class=\"cf\">return<\/span> result<\/span>\n<span id=\"cb1-43\"><a href=\"#cb1-43\" aria-hidden=\"true\" tabindex=\"-1\"><\/a><\/span>\n<span id=\"cb1-44\"><a href=\"#cb1-44\" aria-hidden=\"true\" tabindex=\"-1\"><\/a><\/span>\n<span id=\"cb1-45\"><a href=\"#cb1-45\" aria-hidden=\"true\" tabindex=\"-1\"><\/a>head <span class=\"op\">=<\/span> <span class=\"va\">None<\/span><\/span>\n<span id=\"cb1-46\"><a href=\"#cb1-46\" aria-hidden=\"true\" tabindex=\"-1\"><\/a>head <span class=\"op\">=<\/span> insert_at(head, <span class=\"dv\">0<\/span>, <span class=\"dv\">4<\/span>)<\/span>\n<span id=\"cb1-47\"><a href=\"#cb1-47\" aria-hidden=\"true\" tabindex=\"-1\"><\/a>head <span class=\"op\">=<\/span> insert_at(head, <span class=\"dv\">1<\/span>, <span class=\"dv\">9<\/span>)<\/span>\n<span id=\"cb1-48\"><a href=\"#cb1-48\" aria-hidden=\"true\" tabindex=\"-1\"><\/a>head <span class=\"op\">=<\/span> insert_at(head, <span class=\"dv\">1<\/span>, <span class=\"dv\">7<\/span>)<\/span>\n<span id=\"cb1-49\"><a href=\"#cb1-49\" aria-hidden=\"true\" tabindex=\"-1\"><\/a><span class=\"cf\">assert<\/span> values(head) <span class=\"op\">==<\/span> [<span class=\"dv\">4<\/span>, <span class=\"dv\">7<\/span>, <span class=\"dv\">9<\/span>]<\/span>\n<span id=\"cb1-50\"><a href=\"#cb1-50\" aria-hidden=\"true\" tabindex=\"-1\"><\/a><span class=\"cf\">assert<\/span> contains(head, <span class=\"dv\">7<\/span>) <span class=\"kw\">and<\/span> length(head) <span class=\"op\">==<\/span> <span class=\"dv\">3<\/span><\/span>\n<span id=\"cb1-51\"><a href=\"#cb1-51\" aria-hidden=\"true\" tabindex=\"-1\"><\/a>head <span class=\"op\">=<\/span> remove_first(head, <span class=\"dv\">4<\/span>)<\/span>\n<span id=\"cb1-52\"><a href=\"#cb1-52\" aria-hidden=\"true\" tabindex=\"-1\"><\/a><span class=\"cf\">assert<\/span> values(head) <span class=\"op\">==<\/span> [<span class=\"dv\">7<\/span>, <span class=\"dv\">9<\/span>]<\/span><\/code><\/pre><\/div>\n<h2 id=\"S5\"><span class=\"section-number\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><\/span>Why the procedures work<\/h2>\n<p>For <code>contains<\/code>, an empty list is the unsuccessful base\ncase. Otherwise the head matches, or the search moves to the shorter\nremainder. For <code>insert_at<\/code>, position 0 creates the new chain\nimmediately. At position i &gt; 0, insertion occurs at position i−1 in\nthe remainder; its returned head is reconnected. The same idea applies\nto <code>remove_first<\/code>: a match returns the remainder; otherwise\nthe head is retained and the remainder is processed. <code>length<\/code>\nadds one per node. Decreasing remaining length guarantees termination\nfor finite acyclic lists; cyclic references violate the invariant.<\/p>\n<p>An object-oriented alternative could use an abstract list component\nwith two implementations: an empty list and a data node with a remaining\nlist. This Composite design allows recursive methods without an explicit\n<code>None<\/code> terminator. Our small design uses <code>None<\/code>\ninstead; it is not a complete implementation of the pattern.<\/p>\n<h2 id=\"S6\"><span class=\"section-number\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><\/span>Cost, testing and alternatives<\/h2>\n<p>For n nodes, an unsuccessful search needs n value comparisons, or\nO(n) time. Access to position i costs O(i+1); insertion at the head\ntakes O(1) time. Given a known predecessor node, reference changes also\ntake O(1) time. In this implementation deep recursive calls require O(n)\nextra stack space and may reach Python’s recursion limit. An iterative\nsearch requires only O(1) extra space. By contrast, a Python list\nprovides direct indexed access and may shift many references when\ninserting in the middle. It is not a singly linked list.<\/p>\n<p>Test <code>None<\/code>, position 0, position n, position n+1,\nduplicate values and removal of an absent value. For testing,\n<code>values<\/code> converts the linked structure into a Python list; a\nlarge program should not make the list itself depend on that inspection\noperation.<\/p>\n<h2 id=\"S7\"><span class=\"section-number\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><\/span>Self-assessment<\/h2>\n<h3 id=\"exercises\"><span class=\"section-number\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><\/span>Exercises<\/h3>\n<ol type=\"1\" class=\"lc-content-list\" role=\"list\">\n<li role=\"listitem\"><span class=\"lc-item-marker\" aria-hidden=\"true\">1.<\/span><div class=\"lc-item-content\">Draw [4, 9] and insert 7 at position 1. Which references\nchange?<\/div><\/li>\n<li role=\"listitem\"><span class=\"lc-item-marker\" aria-hidden=\"true\">2.<\/span><div class=\"lc-item-content\">What do <code>length(None)<\/code> and <code>contains(None, 4)<\/code>\nreturn?<\/div><\/li>\n<li role=\"listitem\"><span class=\"lc-item-marker\" aria-hidden=\"true\">3.<\/span><div class=\"lc-item-content\">Remove value 2 once from [2, 2, 5]. What remains?<\/div><\/li>\n<li role=\"listitem\"><span class=\"lc-item-marker\" aria-hidden=\"true\">4.<\/span><div class=\"lc-item-content\">How many comparisons does an unsuccessful search need in a 20-node\nlist?<\/div><\/li>\n<li role=\"listitem\"><span class=\"lc-item-marker\" aria-hidden=\"true\">5.<\/span><div class=\"lc-item-content\">Why is <code>head = insert_at(head, 0, 8)<\/code> necessary when the\nlist is empty?<\/div><\/li>\n<\/ol>\n<details class=\"lc-solutions\" data-lc-section=\"S7\"><summary>Show solutions<\/summary>\n<div>\n<ol type=\"1\" class=\"lc-content-list\" role=\"list\">\n<li role=\"listitem\"><span class=\"lc-item-marker\" aria-hidden=\"true\">1.<\/span><div class=\"lc-item-content\">The new node 7 points to 9, then node 4 points to 7; the head\nremains unchanged.<\/div><\/li>\n<li role=\"listitem\"><span class=\"lc-item-marker\" aria-hidden=\"true\">2.<\/span><div class=\"lc-item-content\">0 and False.<\/div><\/li>\n<li role=\"listitem\"><span class=\"lc-item-marker\" aria-hidden=\"true\">3.<\/span><div class=\"lc-item-content\">[2, 5]; only the first match is removed.<\/div><\/li>\n<li role=\"listitem\"><span class=\"lc-item-marker\" aria-hidden=\"true\">4.<\/span><div class=\"lc-item-content\">20; each node is checked once.<\/div><\/li>\n<li role=\"listitem\"><span class=\"lc-item-marker\" aria-hidden=\"true\">5.<\/span><div class=\"lc-item-content\">The returned value is the reference to the new head. Without\nassignment, <code>head<\/code> remains <code>None<\/code>.<\/div><\/li>\n<\/ol>\n<\/div>\n<\/details>\n<h2 id=\"S8\"><span class=\"section-number\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><\/span>Sources<\/h2>\n<ul class=\"lc-content-list\" role=\"list\">\n<li role=\"listitem\"><span class=\"lc-item-marker\" aria-hidden=\"true\">•<\/span><div class=\"lc-item-content\"><a\nhref=\"https://www.lehrplanplus.bayern.de/fachlehrplan/gymnasium/12/informatik/grundlegend\">LehrplanPLUS\nBayern – Informatik 12 (gA)<span class=\"lc-external-arrow\" aria-hidden=\"true\">&#8239;↗<\/span><span class=\"sr-only lc-external-hint\"> (external link)<\/span><\/a> · Inf12 Lernbereich 2 · Last accessed:\n2026-11-24 · Content verified: 2026-11-24<\/div><\/li>\n<li role=\"listitem\"><span class=\"lc-item-marker\" aria-hidden=\"true\">•<\/span><div class=\"lc-item-content\"><a\nhref=\"https://runestone.academy/ns/books/published/pythonds3/BasicDS/ImplementinganUnorderedListLinkedLists.html\">Runestone\n– Implementing an Unordered List<span class=\"lc-external-arrow\" aria-hidden=\"true\">&#8239;↗<\/span><span class=\"sr-only lc-external-hint\"> (external link)<\/span><\/a> · 3.21 · Last accessed: 2026-11-24\n· Content verified: 2026-11-24<\/div><\/li>\n<\/ul>\n<\/article>","school_computer_science_en:M11-L2":"<article class=\"lesson-standard\"><h1 id=\"L2\">M11-L2 – Binary search trees and traversal<\/h1>\n<p><strong>Course area:<\/strong> M11 – Linked structures and graph search<\/p>\n<p><strong>Level:<\/strong> Upper secondary (basic level)<\/p>\n<p><strong>Prior knowledge:<\/strong> <a\nhref=\"index.html?course=school_computer-science&amp;module=M11&amp;lesson=L1&amp;syslang=en&amp;doclang=en&amp;theme=light\">M11-L1<\/a>; <a\nhref=\"index.html?course=school_computer-science&amp;module=M6&amp;lesson=L5&amp;syslang=en&amp;doclang=en&amp;theme=light\">M6-L5<\/a><\/p>\n<p><strong>Curriculum context:<\/strong> Basic-level extension based on\nBavaria’s Grade 12 curriculum; not a nationwide uniform requirement.<\/p>\n<h2 id=\"S1\"><span class=\"section-number\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><\/span>Learning objectives<\/h2>\n<p>Distinguish a binary tree from a binary search tree, state its\nordering invariant, implement insertion and search, and apply preorder,\ninorder and postorder. Compare the number of key checks with a linked\nlist and explain the effect of tree height.<\/p>\n<h2 id=\"S2\"><span class=\"section-number\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><\/span>Tree structure and ordering<\/h2>\n<p>A binary tree has nodes with at most two ordered child positions,\nleft and right. The root has no parent; a leaf has no children. Height h\nis the maximum number of edges on a path from the root to a leaf; a\nsingle node has height 0. For a search tree with distinct keys, at each\nnode every key in the left subtree is smaller and every key in the right\nsubtree is larger. This rule concerns all descendants, not just\nimmediate children. Payloads may be stored separately from keys. An\narbitrary binary tree need not be a search tree.<\/p>\n<h2 id=\"S3\"><span class=\"section-number\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><\/span>Insertion, search and tree shape<\/h2>\n<p>The sequence 6, 3, 9, 1, 4, 8, 11 creates a tree of height 2. To find\n8, compare with 6, 9 and 8. Searching for 5 follows 6 → 3 → 4 → empty.\nInsertion makes the same decisions and replaces an empty reference by a\nnew node. This model ignores duplicate keys; other applications may\nupdate a count or payload.<\/p>\n<p>Inserting the sorted sequence 1, 3, 4, 6, 8, 9, 11 instead creates a\nright-only chain of height 6. None of these insertion rules balances the\ntree automatically.<\/p>\n<figure>\n<img src=\"../learning-courses-school-computer-science-en/media/img/S_COS_047_EN.svg\"\nalt=\"Left: perfect tree rooted at 6, height 2; right: sorted insertion produces a right chain, height 6.\" />\n<figcaption>Figure: Left: perfect tree rooted at 6, height 2; right:\nsorted insertion produces a right chain, height 6.<\/figcaption>\n<\/figure>\n<h2 id=\"S4\"><span class=\"section-number\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><\/span>Implementation and traversal<\/h2>\n<p>As with linked lists, <code>insert<\/code> returns a possibly new\nsubtree root. <code>search<\/code> is iterative here; a recursive call\ncould process the same smaller subtree at each step. In\n<code>walk<\/code>, the position of the visit relative to the two\nrecursive calls determines the order. <code>order<\/code> must be pre, in\nor post. The accumulator <code>result<\/code> avoids repeatedly copying\npartial lists.<\/p>\n<div class=\"sourceCode\" id=\"cb1\"><pre\nclass=\"sourceCode python\"><code class=\"sourceCode python\"><span id=\"cb1-1\"><a href=\"#cb1-1\" aria-hidden=\"true\" tabindex=\"-1\"><\/a><span class=\"kw\">class<\/span> TreeNode:<\/span>\n<span id=\"cb1-2\"><a href=\"#cb1-2\" aria-hidden=\"true\" tabindex=\"-1\"><\/a>    <span class=\"kw\">def<\/span> <span class=\"fu\">__init__<\/span>(<span class=\"va\">self<\/span>, key):<\/span>\n<span id=\"cb1-3\"><a href=\"#cb1-3\" aria-hidden=\"true\" tabindex=\"-1\"><\/a>        <span class=\"va\">self<\/span>.key <span class=\"op\">=<\/span> key<\/span>\n<span id=\"cb1-4\"><a href=\"#cb1-4\" aria-hidden=\"true\" tabindex=\"-1\"><\/a>        <span class=\"va\">self<\/span>.left <span class=\"op\">=<\/span> <span class=\"va\">None<\/span><\/span>\n<span id=\"cb1-5\"><a href=\"#cb1-5\" aria-hidden=\"true\" tabindex=\"-1\"><\/a>        <span class=\"va\">self<\/span>.right <span class=\"op\">=<\/span> <span class=\"va\">None<\/span><\/span>\n<span id=\"cb1-6\"><a href=\"#cb1-6\" aria-hidden=\"true\" tabindex=\"-1\"><\/a><\/span>\n<span id=\"cb1-7\"><a href=\"#cb1-7\" aria-hidden=\"true\" tabindex=\"-1\"><\/a><\/span>\n<span id=\"cb1-8\"><a href=\"#cb1-8\" aria-hidden=\"true\" tabindex=\"-1\"><\/a><span class=\"kw\">def<\/span> insert(node, key):<\/span>\n<span id=\"cb1-9\"><a href=\"#cb1-9\" aria-hidden=\"true\" tabindex=\"-1\"><\/a>    <span class=\"cf\">if<\/span> node <span class=\"kw\">is<\/span> <span class=\"va\">None<\/span>:<\/span>\n<span id=\"cb1-10\"><a href=\"#cb1-10\" aria-hidden=\"true\" tabindex=\"-1\"><\/a>        <span class=\"cf\">return<\/span> TreeNode(key)<\/span>\n<span id=\"cb1-11\"><a href=\"#cb1-11\" aria-hidden=\"true\" tabindex=\"-1\"><\/a>    <span class=\"cf\">if<\/span> key <span class=\"op\">&lt;<\/span> node.key:<\/span>\n<span id=\"cb1-12\"><a href=\"#cb1-12\" aria-hidden=\"true\" tabindex=\"-1\"><\/a>        node.left <span class=\"op\">=<\/span> insert(node.left, key)<\/span>\n<span id=\"cb1-13\"><a href=\"#cb1-13\" aria-hidden=\"true\" tabindex=\"-1\"><\/a>    <span class=\"cf\">elif<\/span> key <span class=\"op\">&gt;<\/span> node.key:<\/span>\n<span id=\"cb1-14\"><a href=\"#cb1-14\" aria-hidden=\"true\" tabindex=\"-1\"><\/a>        node.right <span class=\"op\">=<\/span> insert(node.right, key)<\/span>\n<span id=\"cb1-15\"><a href=\"#cb1-15\" aria-hidden=\"true\" tabindex=\"-1\"><\/a>    <span class=\"cf\">return<\/span> node<\/span>\n<span id=\"cb1-16\"><a href=\"#cb1-16\" aria-hidden=\"true\" tabindex=\"-1\"><\/a><\/span>\n<span id=\"cb1-17\"><a href=\"#cb1-17\" aria-hidden=\"true\" tabindex=\"-1\"><\/a><\/span>\n<span id=\"cb1-18\"><a href=\"#cb1-18\" aria-hidden=\"true\" tabindex=\"-1\"><\/a><span class=\"kw\">def<\/span> search(node, key):<\/span>\n<span id=\"cb1-19\"><a href=\"#cb1-19\" aria-hidden=\"true\" tabindex=\"-1\"><\/a>    <span class=\"cf\">while<\/span> node <span class=\"kw\">is<\/span> <span class=\"kw\">not<\/span> <span class=\"va\">None<\/span>:<\/span>\n<span id=\"cb1-20\"><a href=\"#cb1-20\" aria-hidden=\"true\" tabindex=\"-1\"><\/a>        <span class=\"cf\">if<\/span> key <span class=\"op\">==<\/span> node.key:<\/span>\n<span id=\"cb1-21\"><a href=\"#cb1-21\" aria-hidden=\"true\" tabindex=\"-1\"><\/a>            <span class=\"cf\">return<\/span> <span class=\"va\">True<\/span><\/span>\n<span id=\"cb1-22\"><a href=\"#cb1-22\" aria-hidden=\"true\" tabindex=\"-1\"><\/a>        node <span class=\"op\">=<\/span> node.left <span class=\"cf\">if<\/span> key <span class=\"op\">&lt;<\/span> node.key <span class=\"cf\">else<\/span> node.right<\/span>\n<span id=\"cb1-23\"><a href=\"#cb1-23\" aria-hidden=\"true\" tabindex=\"-1\"><\/a>    <span class=\"cf\">return<\/span> <span class=\"va\">False<\/span><\/span>\n<span id=\"cb1-24\"><a href=\"#cb1-24\" aria-hidden=\"true\" tabindex=\"-1\"><\/a><\/span>\n<span id=\"cb1-25\"><a href=\"#cb1-25\" aria-hidden=\"true\" tabindex=\"-1\"><\/a><\/span>\n<span id=\"cb1-26\"><a href=\"#cb1-26\" aria-hidden=\"true\" tabindex=\"-1\"><\/a><span class=\"kw\">def<\/span> walk(node, order, result):<\/span>\n<span id=\"cb1-27\"><a href=\"#cb1-27\" aria-hidden=\"true\" tabindex=\"-1\"><\/a>    <span class=\"cf\">if<\/span> node <span class=\"kw\">is<\/span> <span class=\"va\">None<\/span>:<\/span>\n<span id=\"cb1-28\"><a href=\"#cb1-28\" aria-hidden=\"true\" tabindex=\"-1\"><\/a>        <span class=\"cf\">return<\/span><\/span>\n<span id=\"cb1-29\"><a href=\"#cb1-29\" aria-hidden=\"true\" tabindex=\"-1\"><\/a>    <span class=\"cf\">if<\/span> order <span class=\"op\">==<\/span> <span class=\"st\">&quot;pre&quot;<\/span>:<\/span>\n<span id=\"cb1-30\"><a href=\"#cb1-30\" aria-hidden=\"true\" tabindex=\"-1\"><\/a>        result.append(node.key)<\/span>\n<span id=\"cb1-31\"><a href=\"#cb1-31\" aria-hidden=\"true\" tabindex=\"-1\"><\/a>    walk(node.left, order, result)<\/span>\n<span id=\"cb1-32\"><a href=\"#cb1-32\" aria-hidden=\"true\" tabindex=\"-1\"><\/a>    <span class=\"cf\">if<\/span> order <span class=\"op\">==<\/span> <span class=\"st\">&quot;in&quot;<\/span>:<\/span>\n<span id=\"cb1-33\"><a href=\"#cb1-33\" aria-hidden=\"true\" tabindex=\"-1\"><\/a>        result.append(node.key)<\/span>\n<span id=\"cb1-34\"><a href=\"#cb1-34\" aria-hidden=\"true\" tabindex=\"-1\"><\/a>    walk(node.right, order, result)<\/span>\n<span id=\"cb1-35\"><a href=\"#cb1-35\" aria-hidden=\"true\" tabindex=\"-1\"><\/a>    <span class=\"cf\">if<\/span> order <span class=\"op\">==<\/span> <span class=\"st\">&quot;post&quot;<\/span>:<\/span>\n<span id=\"cb1-36\"><a href=\"#cb1-36\" aria-hidden=\"true\" tabindex=\"-1\"><\/a>        result.append(node.key)<\/span>\n<span id=\"cb1-37\"><a href=\"#cb1-37\" aria-hidden=\"true\" tabindex=\"-1\"><\/a><\/span>\n<span id=\"cb1-38\"><a href=\"#cb1-38\" aria-hidden=\"true\" tabindex=\"-1\"><\/a><\/span>\n<span id=\"cb1-39\"><a href=\"#cb1-39\" aria-hidden=\"true\" tabindex=\"-1\"><\/a>root <span class=\"op\">=<\/span> <span class=\"va\">None<\/span><\/span>\n<span id=\"cb1-40\"><a href=\"#cb1-40\" aria-hidden=\"true\" tabindex=\"-1\"><\/a><span class=\"cf\">for<\/span> key <span class=\"kw\">in<\/span> [<span class=\"dv\">6<\/span>, <span class=\"dv\">3<\/span>, <span class=\"dv\">9<\/span>, <span class=\"dv\">1<\/span>, <span class=\"dv\">4<\/span>, <span class=\"dv\">8<\/span>, <span class=\"dv\">11<\/span>]:<\/span>\n<span id=\"cb1-41\"><a href=\"#cb1-41\" aria-hidden=\"true\" tabindex=\"-1\"><\/a>    root <span class=\"op\">=<\/span> insert(root, key)<\/span>\n<span id=\"cb1-42\"><a href=\"#cb1-42\" aria-hidden=\"true\" tabindex=\"-1\"><\/a><span class=\"cf\">for<\/span> order, expected <span class=\"kw\">in<\/span> [<\/span>\n<span id=\"cb1-43\"><a href=\"#cb1-43\" aria-hidden=\"true\" tabindex=\"-1\"><\/a>    (<span class=\"st\">&quot;pre&quot;<\/span>, [<span class=\"dv\">6<\/span>, <span class=\"dv\">3<\/span>, <span class=\"dv\">1<\/span>, <span class=\"dv\">4<\/span>, <span class=\"dv\">9<\/span>, <span class=\"dv\">8<\/span>, <span class=\"dv\">11<\/span>]),<\/span>\n<span id=\"cb1-44\"><a href=\"#cb1-44\" aria-hidden=\"true\" tabindex=\"-1\"><\/a>    (<span class=\"st\">&quot;in&quot;<\/span>, [<span class=\"dv\">1<\/span>, <span class=\"dv\">3<\/span>, <span class=\"dv\">4<\/span>, <span class=\"dv\">6<\/span>, <span class=\"dv\">8<\/span>, <span class=\"dv\">9<\/span>, <span class=\"dv\">11<\/span>]),<\/span>\n<span id=\"cb1-45\"><a href=\"#cb1-45\" aria-hidden=\"true\" tabindex=\"-1\"><\/a>    (<span class=\"st\">&quot;post&quot;<\/span>, [<span class=\"dv\">1<\/span>, <span class=\"dv\">4<\/span>, <span class=\"dv\">3<\/span>, <span class=\"dv\">8<\/span>, <span class=\"dv\">11<\/span>, <span class=\"dv\">9<\/span>, <span class=\"dv\">6<\/span>]),<\/span>\n<span id=\"cb1-46\"><a href=\"#cb1-46\" aria-hidden=\"true\" tabindex=\"-1\"><\/a>]:<\/span>\n<span id=\"cb1-47\"><a href=\"#cb1-47\" aria-hidden=\"true\" tabindex=\"-1\"><\/a>    result <span class=\"op\">=<\/span> []<\/span>\n<span id=\"cb1-48\"><a href=\"#cb1-48\" aria-hidden=\"true\" tabindex=\"-1\"><\/a>    walk(root, order, result)<\/span>\n<span id=\"cb1-49\"><a href=\"#cb1-49\" aria-hidden=\"true\" tabindex=\"-1\"><\/a>    <span class=\"cf\">assert<\/span> result <span class=\"op\">==<\/span> expected<\/span>\n<span id=\"cb1-50\"><a href=\"#cb1-50\" aria-hidden=\"true\" tabindex=\"-1\"><\/a><span class=\"cf\">assert<\/span> search(root, <span class=\"dv\">8<\/span>) <span class=\"kw\">and<\/span> <span class=\"kw\">not<\/span> search(root, <span class=\"dv\">5<\/span>)<\/span><\/code><\/pre><\/div>\n<h2 id=\"S5\"><span class=\"section-number\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><\/span>Correctness and applications<\/h2>\n<p>The ordering invariant excludes an entire subtree at each comparison.\nReconnecting the new subtree root at the same child position preserves\nthe bounds imposed by its ancestors. An empty subtree is the base case.\nInorder visits left, node, right; by the invariant its output is\nstrictly increasing. Preorder visits the node before its subtrees, for\nexample to present a hierarchy. Postorder visits it after both subtrees,\nfor instance to evaluate an expression tree from its operands. Preorder\nalone cannot reconstruct an arbitrary binary tree without structural\ninformation.<\/p>\n<p>As in <a href=\"index.html?course=school_computer-science&amp;module=M11&amp;lesson=L1&amp;syslang=en&amp;doclang=en&amp;theme=light\">M11-L1<\/a>, a Composite\ndesign could model empty and nonempty subtrees through a shared\ninterface; here <code>None<\/code> represents empty subtrees.<\/p>\n<h2 id=\"S6\"><span class=\"section-number\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><\/span>Cost and limitations<\/h2>\n<p>Counting one abstract three-way key comparison per examined node, at\nmost h+1 nodes need to be checked. A perfect binary tree of height h has\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><msup><mn>2<\/mn><mrow><mi>h<\/mi><mo>+<\/mo><mn>1<\/mn><\/mrow><\/msup><mo>−<\/mo><mn>1<\/mn><\/mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">2^{h+1}-1<\/annotation><\/semantics><\/math>\nnodes. In an appropriately balanced structure h grows logarithmically\nwith n, so search and insertion cost O(log n). A degenerate chain can\nrequire n checks in the worst case, like a linked list. The code does\nnot count individual Python comparison operators, which may execute more\nthan once per node. Each full traversal visits n nodes, needs O(n) time\nand uses O(h+1) call stack space in addition to the output. For large\ndatasets, self-balancing trees or other index structures may be\nappropriate. An ordinary search tree does not promise logarithmic\nworst-case time.<\/p>\n<h2 id=\"S7\"><span class=\"section-number\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><\/span>Self-assessment<\/h2>\n<h3 id=\"exercises\"><span class=\"section-number\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><\/span>Exercises<\/h3>\n<ol type=\"1\" class=\"lc-content-list\" role=\"list\">\n<li role=\"listitem\"><span class=\"lc-item-marker\" aria-hidden=\"true\">1.<\/span><div class=\"lc-item-content\">Insert 5 into the example tree. Where does it go?<\/div><\/li>\n<li role=\"listitem\"><span class=\"lc-item-marker\" aria-hidden=\"true\">2.<\/span><div class=\"lc-item-content\">Give the inorder and preorder sequences of the example tree.<\/div><\/li>\n<li role=\"listitem\"><span class=\"lc-item-marker\" aria-hidden=\"true\">3.<\/span><div class=\"lc-item-content\">A tree has root 6, left child 3 and the latter’s right child 7. Is\nit a search tree?<\/div><\/li>\n<li role=\"listitem\"><span class=\"lc-item-marker\" aria-hidden=\"true\">4.<\/span><div class=\"lc-item-content\">Compare maximum node checks for the two illustrated trees and a\nseven-node list.<\/div><\/li>\n<li role=\"listitem\"><span class=\"lc-item-marker\" aria-hidden=\"true\">5.<\/span><div class=\"lc-item-content\">Why can inserting sorted keys into an ordinary search tree be\nundesirable?<\/div><\/li>\n<\/ol>\n<details class=\"lc-solutions\" data-lc-section=\"S7\"><summary>Show solutions<\/summary>\n<div>\n<ol type=\"1\" class=\"lc-content-list\" role=\"list\">\n<li role=\"listitem\"><span class=\"lc-item-marker\" aria-hidden=\"true\">1.<\/span><div class=\"lc-item-content\">Right child of 4; path 6 → 3 → 4 → right.<\/div><\/li>\n<li role=\"listitem\"><span class=\"lc-item-marker\" aria-hidden=\"true\">2.<\/span><div class=\"lc-item-content\">Inorder: 1, 3, 4, 6, 8, 9, 11; preorder: 6, 3, 1, 4, 9, 8, 11.<\/div><\/li>\n<li role=\"listitem\"><span class=\"lc-item-marker\" aria-hidden=\"true\">3.<\/span><div class=\"lc-item-content\">No. 7 belongs to the left subtree of 6 but is not smaller than\n6.<\/div><\/li>\n<li role=\"listitem\"><span class=\"lc-item-marker\" aria-hidden=\"true\">4.<\/span><div class=\"lc-item-content\">3 in the perfect tree, 7 in the right chain and up to 7 in the\nlist.<\/div><\/li>\n<li role=\"listitem\"><span class=\"lc-item-marker\" aria-hidden=\"true\">5.<\/span><div class=\"lc-item-content\">Each new key goes to the right of the former maximum. Height grows\nlinearly, so worst-case search becomes linear.<\/div><\/li>\n<\/ol>\n<\/div>\n<\/details>\n<h2 id=\"S8\"><span class=\"section-number\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><\/span>Sources<\/h2>\n<ul class=\"lc-content-list\" role=\"list\">\n<li role=\"listitem\"><span class=\"lc-item-marker\" aria-hidden=\"true\">•<\/span><div class=\"lc-item-content\"><a\nhref=\"https://www.lehrplanplus.bayern.de/fachlehrplan/gymnasium/12/informatik/grundlegend\">LehrplanPLUS\nBayern – Informatik 12 (gA)<span class=\"lc-external-arrow\" aria-hidden=\"true\">&#8239;↗<\/span><span class=\"sr-only lc-external-hint\"> (external link)<\/span><\/a> · Inf12 Lernbereich 3 · Last accessed:\n2026-11-24 · Content verified: 2026-11-24<\/div><\/li>\n<li role=\"listitem\"><span class=\"lc-item-marker\" aria-hidden=\"true\">•<\/span><div class=\"lc-item-content\"><a\nhref=\"https://runestone.academy/ns/books/published/pythonds3/Trees/TreeTraversals.html\">Runestone\n– Tree Traversals<span class=\"lc-external-arrow\" aria-hidden=\"true\">&#8239;↗<\/span><span class=\"sr-only lc-external-hint\"> (external link)<\/span><\/a> · 6.8 · Last accessed: 2026-11-24 · Content\nverified: 2026-11-24<\/div><\/li>\n<li role=\"listitem\"><span class=\"lc-item-marker\" aria-hidden=\"true\">•<\/span><div class=\"lc-item-content\"><a\nhref=\"https://runestone.academy/ns/books/published/pythonds3/Trees/SearchTreeAnalysis.html\">Runestone\n– Search Tree Analysis<span class=\"lc-external-arrow\" aria-hidden=\"true\">&#8239;↗<\/span><span class=\"sr-only lc-external-hint\"> (external link)<\/span><\/a> · 6.15 · Last accessed: 2026-11-24 · Content\nverified: 2026-11-24<\/div><\/li>\n<\/ul>\n<\/article>","school_computer_science_en:M11-L3":"<article class=\"lesson-standard\"><h1 id=\"L3\">M11-L3 – Depth-first search and reachable vertices<\/h1>\n<p><strong>Course area:<\/strong> M11 – Linked structures and graph search<\/p>\n<p><strong>Level:<\/strong> Upper secondary (basic level)<\/p>\n<p><strong>Prior knowledge:<\/strong> <a\nhref=\"index.html?course=school_computer-science&amp;module=M6&amp;lesson=L4&amp;syslang=en&amp;doclang=en&amp;theme=light\">M6-L4<\/a>; <a\nhref=\"index.html?course=school_computer-science&amp;module=M6&amp;lesson=L5&amp;syslang=en&amp;doclang=en&amp;theme=light\">M6-L5<\/a><\/p>\n<p><strong>Curriculum context:<\/strong> Basic-level extension based on\nBavaria’s Grade 12 curriculum; not a nationwide uniform requirement.<\/p>\n<h2 id=\"S1\"><span class=\"section-number\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><\/span>Learning objectives<\/h2>\n<p>Represent directed graphs using adjacency lists, perform depth-first\nsearch (DFS) with a visited set, explain backtracking to pending\nneighbors, and compare DFS with breadth-first search (BFS). Select\nreachable vertices, handle cycles safely and justify the cost.<\/p>\n<h2 id=\"S2\"><span class=\"section-number\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><\/span>Graph and reachability<\/h2>\n<p>A directed graph consists of a vertex set V and directed edge set E.\nEdge A → B allows a step from A to B, but not automatically back. A\nvertex is reachable from start s if a directed path exists from s to it;\ns itself is reachable along a path of length zero. We store each\nvertex’s outgoing neighbors in a fixed order. Every neighbor must also\noccur as a key, even if its own list is empty. Our example has edges A →\nB, A → C, B → D, C → E, D → A and D → E; F is isolated.<\/p>\n<h2 id=\"S3\"><span class=\"section-number\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><\/span>Depth-first search step by step<\/h2>\n<p>Start at A and mark A immediately. Its first neighbor is B, then D. D\nhas A as a neighbor, but A is already marked; D visits E instead. E has\nno neighbors. Recursive calls return one at a time until A processes its\nnext pending neighbor C. C points to the already visited E. The\nvisitation order is A, B, D, E, C. F is not reached. Edge D → A creates\na cycle without trapping the algorithm in an infinite loop.<\/p>\n<figure>\n<img src=\"../learning-courses-school-computer-science-en/media/img/S_COS_048_EN.svg\"\nalt=\"Directed graph with cycle A–B–D–A and isolated F. DFS A B D E C; BFS A B C D E.\" />\n<figcaption>Figure: Directed graph with cycle A–B–D–A and isolated F.\nDFS A B D E C; BFS A B C D E.<\/figcaption>\n<\/figure>\n<h2 id=\"S4\"><span class=\"section-number\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><\/span>Recursive and iterative implementation<\/h2>\n<p>In this Python 3 example the start and all neighbors must be valid\nkeys. Vertices are strings; <code>None<\/code> is not a vertex. The\nexplicit stack version keeps an iterator over pending neighbors at each\nactive level, exactly reproducing the recursive order. The BFS queue\nmarks vertices when they are enqueued.<\/p>\n<div class=\"sourceCode\" id=\"cb1\"><pre\nclass=\"sourceCode python\"><code class=\"sourceCode python\"><span id=\"cb1-1\"><a href=\"#cb1-1\" aria-hidden=\"true\" tabindex=\"-1\"><\/a><span class=\"im\">from<\/span> collections <span class=\"im\">import<\/span> deque<\/span>\n<span id=\"cb1-2\"><a href=\"#cb1-2\" aria-hidden=\"true\" tabindex=\"-1\"><\/a><\/span>\n<span id=\"cb1-3\"><a href=\"#cb1-3\" aria-hidden=\"true\" tabindex=\"-1\"><\/a>graph <span class=\"op\">=<\/span> {<\/span>\n<span id=\"cb1-4\"><a href=\"#cb1-4\" aria-hidden=\"true\" tabindex=\"-1\"><\/a>    <span class=\"st\">&quot;A&quot;<\/span>: [<span class=\"st\">&quot;B&quot;<\/span>, <span class=\"st\">&quot;C&quot;<\/span>], <span class=\"st\">&quot;B&quot;<\/span>: [<span class=\"st\">&quot;D&quot;<\/span>], <span class=\"st\">&quot;C&quot;<\/span>: [<span class=\"st\">&quot;E&quot;<\/span>],<\/span>\n<span id=\"cb1-5\"><a href=\"#cb1-5\" aria-hidden=\"true\" tabindex=\"-1\"><\/a>    <span class=\"st\">&quot;D&quot;<\/span>: [<span class=\"st\">&quot;A&quot;<\/span>, <span class=\"st\">&quot;E&quot;<\/span>], <span class=\"st\">&quot;E&quot;<\/span>: [], <span class=\"st\">&quot;F&quot;<\/span>: []<\/span>\n<span id=\"cb1-6\"><a href=\"#cb1-6\" aria-hidden=\"true\" tabindex=\"-1\"><\/a>}<\/span>\n<span id=\"cb1-7\"><a href=\"#cb1-7\" aria-hidden=\"true\" tabindex=\"-1\"><\/a><\/span>\n<span id=\"cb1-8\"><a href=\"#cb1-8\" aria-hidden=\"true\" tabindex=\"-1\"><\/a><\/span>\n<span id=\"cb1-9\"><a href=\"#cb1-9\" aria-hidden=\"true\" tabindex=\"-1\"><\/a><span class=\"kw\">def<\/span> dfs(graph, start):<\/span>\n<span id=\"cb1-10\"><a href=\"#cb1-10\" aria-hidden=\"true\" tabindex=\"-1\"><\/a>    seen, order <span class=\"op\">=<\/span> <span class=\"bu\">set<\/span>(), []<\/span>\n<span id=\"cb1-11\"><a href=\"#cb1-11\" aria-hidden=\"true\" tabindex=\"-1\"><\/a>    <span class=\"kw\">def<\/span> visit(v):<\/span>\n<span id=\"cb1-12\"><a href=\"#cb1-12\" aria-hidden=\"true\" tabindex=\"-1\"><\/a>        seen.add(v)<\/span>\n<span id=\"cb1-13\"><a href=\"#cb1-13\" aria-hidden=\"true\" tabindex=\"-1\"><\/a>        order.append(v)<\/span>\n<span id=\"cb1-14\"><a href=\"#cb1-14\" aria-hidden=\"true\" tabindex=\"-1\"><\/a>        <span class=\"cf\">for<\/span> w <span class=\"kw\">in<\/span> graph[v]:<\/span>\n<span id=\"cb1-15\"><a href=\"#cb1-15\" aria-hidden=\"true\" tabindex=\"-1\"><\/a>            <span class=\"cf\">if<\/span> w <span class=\"kw\">not<\/span> <span class=\"kw\">in<\/span> seen:<\/span>\n<span id=\"cb1-16\"><a href=\"#cb1-16\" aria-hidden=\"true\" tabindex=\"-1\"><\/a>                visit(w)<\/span>\n<span id=\"cb1-17\"><a href=\"#cb1-17\" aria-hidden=\"true\" tabindex=\"-1\"><\/a>    visit(start)<\/span>\n<span id=\"cb1-18\"><a href=\"#cb1-18\" aria-hidden=\"true\" tabindex=\"-1\"><\/a>    <span class=\"cf\">return<\/span> order<\/span>\n<span id=\"cb1-19\"><a href=\"#cb1-19\" aria-hidden=\"true\" tabindex=\"-1\"><\/a><\/span>\n<span id=\"cb1-20\"><a href=\"#cb1-20\" aria-hidden=\"true\" tabindex=\"-1\"><\/a><\/span>\n<span id=\"cb1-21\"><a href=\"#cb1-21\" aria-hidden=\"true\" tabindex=\"-1\"><\/a><span class=\"kw\">def<\/span> dfs_stack(graph, start):<\/span>\n<span id=\"cb1-22\"><a href=\"#cb1-22\" aria-hidden=\"true\" tabindex=\"-1\"><\/a>    seen, order <span class=\"op\">=<\/span> {start}, [start]<\/span>\n<span id=\"cb1-23\"><a href=\"#cb1-23\" aria-hidden=\"true\" tabindex=\"-1\"><\/a>    stack <span class=\"op\">=<\/span> [<span class=\"bu\">iter<\/span>(graph[start])]<\/span>\n<span id=\"cb1-24\"><a href=\"#cb1-24\" aria-hidden=\"true\" tabindex=\"-1\"><\/a>    <span class=\"cf\">while<\/span> stack:<\/span>\n<span id=\"cb1-25\"><a href=\"#cb1-25\" aria-hidden=\"true\" tabindex=\"-1\"><\/a>        w <span class=\"op\">=<\/span> <span class=\"bu\">next<\/span>(stack[<span class=\"op\">-<\/span><span class=\"dv\">1<\/span>], <span class=\"va\">None<\/span>)<\/span>\n<span id=\"cb1-26\"><a href=\"#cb1-26\" aria-hidden=\"true\" tabindex=\"-1\"><\/a>        <span class=\"cf\">if<\/span> w <span class=\"kw\">is<\/span> <span class=\"va\">None<\/span>:<\/span>\n<span id=\"cb1-27\"><a href=\"#cb1-27\" aria-hidden=\"true\" tabindex=\"-1\"><\/a>            stack.pop()<\/span>\n<span id=\"cb1-28\"><a href=\"#cb1-28\" aria-hidden=\"true\" tabindex=\"-1\"><\/a>        <span class=\"cf\">elif<\/span> w <span class=\"kw\">not<\/span> <span class=\"kw\">in<\/span> seen:<\/span>\n<span id=\"cb1-29\"><a href=\"#cb1-29\" aria-hidden=\"true\" tabindex=\"-1\"><\/a>            seen.add(w)<\/span>\n<span id=\"cb1-30\"><a href=\"#cb1-30\" aria-hidden=\"true\" tabindex=\"-1\"><\/a>            order.append(w)<\/span>\n<span id=\"cb1-31\"><a href=\"#cb1-31\" aria-hidden=\"true\" tabindex=\"-1\"><\/a>            stack.append(<span class=\"bu\">iter<\/span>(graph[w]))<\/span>\n<span id=\"cb1-32\"><a href=\"#cb1-32\" aria-hidden=\"true\" tabindex=\"-1\"><\/a>    <span class=\"cf\">return<\/span> order<\/span>\n<span id=\"cb1-33\"><a href=\"#cb1-33\" aria-hidden=\"true\" tabindex=\"-1\"><\/a><\/span>\n<span id=\"cb1-34\"><a href=\"#cb1-34\" aria-hidden=\"true\" tabindex=\"-1\"><\/a><\/span>\n<span id=\"cb1-35\"><a href=\"#cb1-35\" aria-hidden=\"true\" tabindex=\"-1\"><\/a><span class=\"kw\">def<\/span> bfs(graph, start):<\/span>\n<span id=\"cb1-36\"><a href=\"#cb1-36\" aria-hidden=\"true\" tabindex=\"-1\"><\/a>    seen, order <span class=\"op\">=<\/span> {start}, []<\/span>\n<span id=\"cb1-37\"><a href=\"#cb1-37\" aria-hidden=\"true\" tabindex=\"-1\"><\/a>    queue <span class=\"op\">=<\/span> deque([start])<\/span>\n<span id=\"cb1-38\"><a href=\"#cb1-38\" aria-hidden=\"true\" tabindex=\"-1\"><\/a>    <span class=\"cf\">while<\/span> queue:<\/span>\n<span id=\"cb1-39\"><a href=\"#cb1-39\" aria-hidden=\"true\" tabindex=\"-1\"><\/a>        v <span class=\"op\">=<\/span> queue.popleft()<\/span>\n<span id=\"cb1-40\"><a href=\"#cb1-40\" aria-hidden=\"true\" tabindex=\"-1\"><\/a>        order.append(v)<\/span>\n<span id=\"cb1-41\"><a href=\"#cb1-41\" aria-hidden=\"true\" tabindex=\"-1\"><\/a>        <span class=\"cf\">for<\/span> w <span class=\"kw\">in<\/span> graph[v]:<\/span>\n<span id=\"cb1-42\"><a href=\"#cb1-42\" aria-hidden=\"true\" tabindex=\"-1\"><\/a>            <span class=\"cf\">if<\/span> w <span class=\"kw\">not<\/span> <span class=\"kw\">in<\/span> seen:<\/span>\n<span id=\"cb1-43\"><a href=\"#cb1-43\" aria-hidden=\"true\" tabindex=\"-1\"><\/a>                seen.add(w)<\/span>\n<span id=\"cb1-44\"><a href=\"#cb1-44\" aria-hidden=\"true\" tabindex=\"-1\"><\/a>                queue.append(w)<\/span>\n<span id=\"cb1-45\"><a href=\"#cb1-45\" aria-hidden=\"true\" tabindex=\"-1\"><\/a>    <span class=\"cf\">return<\/span> order<\/span>\n<span id=\"cb1-46\"><a href=\"#cb1-46\" aria-hidden=\"true\" tabindex=\"-1\"><\/a><\/span>\n<span id=\"cb1-47\"><a href=\"#cb1-47\" aria-hidden=\"true\" tabindex=\"-1\"><\/a><\/span>\n<span id=\"cb1-48\"><a href=\"#cb1-48\" aria-hidden=\"true\" tabindex=\"-1\"><\/a><span class=\"cf\">assert<\/span> dfs(graph, <span class=\"st\">&quot;A&quot;<\/span>) <span class=\"op\">==<\/span> [<span class=\"st\">&quot;A&quot;<\/span>, <span class=\"st\">&quot;B&quot;<\/span>, <span class=\"st\">&quot;D&quot;<\/span>, <span class=\"st\">&quot;E&quot;<\/span>, <span class=\"st\">&quot;C&quot;<\/span>]<\/span>\n<span id=\"cb1-49\"><a href=\"#cb1-49\" aria-hidden=\"true\" tabindex=\"-1\"><\/a><span class=\"cf\">assert<\/span> dfs_stack(graph, <span class=\"st\">&quot;A&quot;<\/span>) <span class=\"op\">==<\/span> dfs(graph, <span class=\"st\">&quot;A&quot;<\/span>)<\/span>\n<span id=\"cb1-50\"><a href=\"#cb1-50\" aria-hidden=\"true\" tabindex=\"-1\"><\/a><span class=\"cf\">assert<\/span> bfs(graph, <span class=\"st\">&quot;A&quot;<\/span>) <span class=\"op\">==<\/span> [<span class=\"st\">&quot;A&quot;<\/span>, <span class=\"st\">&quot;B&quot;<\/span>, <span class=\"st\">&quot;C&quot;<\/span>, <span class=\"st\">&quot;D&quot;<\/span>, <span class=\"st\">&quot;E&quot;<\/span>]<\/span><\/code><\/pre><\/div>\n<h2 id=\"S5\"><span class=\"section-number\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><\/span>Correctness and cost<\/h2>\n<p>Each newly marked vertex is discovered along an edge from a reachable\nvertex, and is therefore reachable. If a reachable vertex remained\nunvisited after termination, a path from the start would contain a first\nedge from a visited to an unvisited vertex; that edge would have been\nexamined when processing the visited vertex. This is a contradiction.\nThe visited set prevents repeat visits; a finite number of vertices and\nedges ensures termination. For V_r reachable vertices and E_r edges\noutgoing from them, expected time is O(V_r+E_r), assuming average\nconstant-time set and dictionary access. Both DFS versions use O(V_r)\nextra space including the visited set and stack, excluding the input\ngraph. Recursion can exceed Python’s call-depth limit; the explicit\nstack avoids that limit.<\/p>\n<h2 id=\"S6\"><span class=\"section-number\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><\/span>Comparison with breadth-first search and applications<\/h2>\n<p>BFS processes neighbors first and here returns A, B, C, D, E. In an\nunweighted graph BFS discovers vertices in nondecreasing distance\n(number of edges) from the start. With predecessor information, BFS can\nreconstruct shortest paths; DFS does not guarantee a shortest path. DFS\nis useful, for instance, to enumerate all linked pages reachable from a\nstarting page.\n<code>selected = [v for v in dfs(graph, \"A\") if v in {\"C\", \"F\"}]<\/code>\nreturns only C: determine reachability first, then check the property.\nFiltering too early during traversal could skip necessary intermediate\nvertices. Both search orders depend on adjacency order. To traverse all\ncomponents, one can start from each still unvisited vertex with a shared\nvisited set. In directed graphs, an edge to an already visited neighbor\nis not alone proof of a cycle; additional state information is\nneeded.<\/p>\n<h2 id=\"S7\"><span class=\"section-number\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><\/span>Self-assessment<\/h2>\n<h3 id=\"exercises\"><span class=\"section-number\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><\/span>Exercises<\/h3>\n<ol type=\"1\" class=\"lc-content-list\" role=\"list\">\n<li role=\"listitem\"><span class=\"lc-item-marker\" aria-hidden=\"true\">1.<\/span><div class=\"lc-item-content\">Which vertices does DFS visit from A and in what order?<\/div><\/li>\n<li role=\"listitem\"><span class=\"lc-item-marker\" aria-hidden=\"true\">2.<\/span><div class=\"lc-item-content\">Which vertices are reachable from C?<\/div><\/li>\n<li role=\"listitem\"><span class=\"lc-item-marker\" aria-hidden=\"true\">3.<\/span><div class=\"lc-item-content\">What happens if the visited set is omitted in this example?<\/div><\/li>\n<li role=\"listitem\"><span class=\"lc-item-marker\" aria-hidden=\"true\">4.<\/span><div class=\"lc-item-content\">What order does BFS produce from A? Which method guarantees minimum\ndistance for unweighted edges?<\/div><\/li>\n<li role=\"listitem\"><span class=\"lc-item-marker\" aria-hidden=\"true\">5.<\/span><div class=\"lc-item-content\">Change A’s neighbors to [C, B]. Give the new DFS order and the set\nof reachable vertices.<\/div><\/li>\n<\/ol>\n<details class=\"lc-solutions\" data-lc-section=\"S7\"><summary>Show solutions<\/summary>\n<div>\n<ol type=\"1\" class=\"lc-content-list\" role=\"list\">\n<li role=\"listitem\"><span class=\"lc-item-marker\" aria-hidden=\"true\">1.<\/span><div class=\"lc-item-content\">A, B, D, E, C.<\/div><\/li>\n<li role=\"listitem\"><span class=\"lc-item-marker\" aria-hidden=\"true\">2.<\/span><div class=\"lc-item-content\">C and E.<\/div><\/li>\n<li role=\"listitem\"><span class=\"lc-item-marker\" aria-hidden=\"true\">3.<\/span><div class=\"lc-item-content\">A → B → D → A repeats; the recursive program may eventually raise a\nrecursion error.<\/div><\/li>\n<li role=\"listitem\"><span class=\"lc-item-marker\" aria-hidden=\"true\">4.<\/span><div class=\"lc-item-content\">A, B, C, D, E; BFS guarantees minimum edge-count distance upon first\ndiscovery.<\/div><\/li>\n<li role=\"listitem\"><span class=\"lc-item-marker\" aria-hidden=\"true\">5.<\/span><div class=\"lc-item-content\">A, C, E, B, D; the same set {A, B, C, D, E}.<\/div><\/li>\n<\/ol>\n<\/div>\n<\/details>\n<h2 id=\"S8\"><span class=\"section-number\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><\/span>Sources<\/h2>\n<ul class=\"lc-content-list\" role=\"list\">\n<li role=\"listitem\"><span class=\"lc-item-marker\" aria-hidden=\"true\">•<\/span><div class=\"lc-item-content\"><a\nhref=\"https://www.lehrplanplus.bayern.de/fachlehrplan/gymnasium/12/informatik/grundlegend\">LehrplanPLUS\nBayern – Informatik 12 (gA)<span class=\"lc-external-arrow\" aria-hidden=\"true\">&#8239;↗<\/span><span class=\"sr-only lc-external-hint\"> (external link)<\/span><\/a> · Inf12 Lernbereich 1 · Last accessed:\n2026-11-24 · Content verified: 2026-11-24<\/div><\/li>\n<li role=\"listitem\"><span class=\"lc-item-marker\" aria-hidden=\"true\">•<\/span><div class=\"lc-item-content\"><a\nhref=\"https://courses.cs.cornell.edu/cs2110/2025fa/lectures/lec22/\">Cornell\nCS 2110 – Graph Traversals<span class=\"lc-external-arrow\" aria-hidden=\"true\">&#8239;↗<\/span><span class=\"sr-only lc-external-hint\"> (external link)<\/span><\/a> · DFS, BFS, Complexity Analysis · Last\naccessed: 2026-11-24 · Content verified: 2026-11-24<\/div><\/li>\n<\/ul>\n<\/article>"};
